# Secrets, domains & deploy safety

## Never commit secrets

- Do **not** hardcode `sbp_…`, service role keys, Resend/R2/OneSignal secrets, or JWTs in `mcp.json`, docs, examples, or source.
- Store personal access tokens only in **gitignored** files (`mcp-config.env`, `.env*`). Prefer `${SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN}` placeholders in committed MCP config.
- If a token was pasted in chat or committed historically: **rotate it** and scrub the file; do not reuse the leaked value.
- Never print full secrets in agent replies; confirm actions by name only (`ALLOWED_ORIGINS` set).

## Supabase Edge secrets

- Update Edge Function secrets via **Management API** or Dashboard — not by embedding values in the repo.
- `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` must include every browser origin that calls functions:
  - `https://www.wya254.com`, `https://wya254.com`, `https://admin.wya254.com`, localhost ports used in dev.
- Public consumer links use `PUBLIC_SITE_URL` / `https://www.wya254.com` (not the admin host).

## Domain split

| Host | Role |
|------|------|
| `www.wya254.com` | Consumer app only |
| `admin.wya254.com` | Admin console only (`/admin`) |
| `cdn.wya254.com` | Media |

- Do not ship admin UI discoverable on the consumer marketing site as the primary entry.
- Admin host must not mount the landing page; consumer `/admin*` redirects to `admin.wya254.com`.
- Client helpers: `src/lib/site-origins.ts` (`VITE_PUBLIC_SITE_URL`, `VITE_ADMIN_SITE_URL`).

## Vercel

- Project **Root Directory** must not be `.` or `./` (causes CLI deploy failure). Leave empty / auto.
- Use `.vercelignore` so CLI deploys do not upload `android/`, `.git`, `.vite`, etc.
- `VITE_*` domain env vars require a **redeploy** after change (build-time).

## Checklist before shipping auth/CORS/domain work

1. No `sbp_` / secret strings in `git grep` on tracked files  
2. `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` includes admin + www + localhost  
3. Smoke: `admin.wya254.com/` → `/admin`; `www…/admin` → admin host  
4. Tokens only in gitignored env files
